# Digest-verified test fixtures.
#
# tests/fixtures/triage-sample/run-manifest.json records a SHA-256 for every file
# beside it, and `analyze` verifies those digests before reading a triage folder.
# Git for Windows enables core.autocrlf by default, so without this rule every
# fixture is rewritten LF -> CRLF on checkout, every digest mismatches, and the
# analysis tests fail on every Windows clone — the platform this tool targets.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion for these files in both directions.
tests/fixtures/** -text
